          <change when="2023-06-06T15:09:15-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/t_m_hickey">Commit - Changed l. 7's οἴκῳ to οἴνῳ. I can see why the ed. read κ, but ν is better palaeographically (cf., e.g., initial letter of l. 4) and sense-wise. I have an unambiguous parallel in a forthcoming ed.: παρασχεῖν αὐτῇ ἐν οἴνῳ. </change>
